    def no_spaces(cls, v):", "replace": "    @field_validator("username")
    @classmethod
    def no_spaces(cls, v):", "explanation": "Per the Pydantic v2 migration guide, `@validator` is deprecated in favor of `@field_validator`, and v2 field validators must be classmethods, so `@classmethod` is added beneath the decorator. The validator body is unchanged and still raises ValueError on spaces."}], "notes": "Applied the v1 `@validator` -> v2 `@field_validator` fix (with `@classmethod`) and updated the import. Not changed, but flagged for follow-up: (1) `MESSAGE_CODES` matches v1 message text. Pydantic v2 uses different wording, e.g. "Field required" (capitalized), "Input should be a valid integer, unable to parse string as an integer", and "String should have at least 3 characters" instead of "ensure this value has at least". The `startswith` lookups will therefore fall through to "INVALID" for these errors. This is a behavior change outside the listed finding, so it needs its own change and tests. Matching on `err["type"]` (e.g. "missing", "int_parsing", "string_too_short") would be more robust. (2) `Field(..., min_length=3)` is valid in v2 and needs no change. No documentation was retrieved, so the citations above rely on general knowledge of the v2 migration guide."}
